==============================================================================
W0  Structural ceiling: unserved energy is policy-invariant
==============================================================================
sum_j D_j(w) <= min(sum_i gbar_i(w), sum_j dbar_j(w)) and VOLL >> mc, so
the planner always serves the physical maximum. Shedding is fixed by the
scenario, not by the policy. Risk-aware clearing can only move the
remaining adjustment cost. This bounds every result that follows.
  [skip] seed=2037: RuntimeError: solve failed: status=user_limit

  max |CVaR[unserved]_aware - CVaR[unserved]_neutral| = 3.411e-13 MW   on a base of 234.35 MW  (relative 1.46e-15)
  -> unserved energy is INVARIANT to the day-ahead policy
  share of tail cost that is unreachable (unserved x VOLL): 76.3%
  reachable tail cost (energy + deviations): 56140.3 of 240965.9

  Read this as the ceiling: a gap quoted as X% of tail cost is
  4.22x that as a share of the cost the policy can actually move.

