==============================================================================
W7  Tail-heaviness of supply -- the central claim
==============================================================================
Claim: tail-heavy supply produces tail-heavy welfare, and risk-aware
clearing is worth more there. Four independent drivers are swept; if
they agree, the result is about tail-heaviness and not about one knob.

Report gap$ and reach% (share of energy + adjustment cost, the part a
day-ahead policy can move). tailcost% is flat BY CONSTRUCTION, because
heavier tails inflate the policy-invariant unserved term in step.

